|~ `::link`, the kind of a link, and the laws declared under it. ~|

:link
  |~~ The kind of a link, a query a page names for its reader to follow,
      written in the prose of a doc as a quote under `::link`.
      Links are what make the pages a hypertext: a page names the pages
      that go deeper, and a reader reaches them by `open`, which runs the
      query the link holds. A link opens a page, so `links | map ~open`
      answers pages alone, and a query that lists or shows something is a
      snippet; a law answers true, and stands under the name it proves.
      Every link of the catalog opens a page. A host may
      stack its own tag over a link.
      ::snippet~(::qlang | doc | links) lists the links of the first page.
      ::link~(::qlang/hypertext | doc)
  ~~|

:link/isALink
  |~~ A link a doc holds is a `::link`. ~~|
  ::law~(|~~ ::link~(::qlang/values | doc) ~~| | links | first | type | eq ::link)

:link/opensToPages
  |~~ The links of the first page open to pages. ~~|
  ::law~(::qlang | doc | links | map ~open | every ~(type | eq ::doc))

:link/holdsUnderAStackOfTags
  |~~ A quote under a stack of tags holding `::link` is a link. ~~|
  ::law~(|~~ ::Host::link~(1) ~~| | links | count | eq 1)
